description:
This PR splits existing `check_*()` functions into two functions: `tbl_check_*()` and `tbl_grade_*()` functions. Closes #15.

`tbl_grade_*()` functions retain the existing characteristics of `check_*()` functions. They detect differences between two objects and return a failing `gradethis` grade with an informative message and attached `problem` object. These functions will likely be used in the majority of cases.

`tbl_check_*()` functions return only the `problem` object without signalling a condition. This allows authors to inspect the problem object to generate custom messages for situations specific to their tutorial or to ignore differences that are irrelevant to their tutorial. `problem` objects generated by `tbl_check_*()` functions can be passed to `tbl_grade()` to retain `tblcheck`'s default messaging functionality (this is how the `tbl_grade_*()` functions are implemented internally). An example use case could be as follows:

````markdown
```{r exercise-check}
grade_this({
  problem <- tbl_check_table()

  if (problem$type == "column_class" && problem$actual == "difftime") {
    fail("I expected you to create a time interval. Did you remember to use `interval()`?")
  } else {
    tbl_grade(problem)
  }
})
```
````

This PR also adds a vignette detailing usage of `tblcheck`, highlighting these changes.
